course: dictionary
lesson: 1022
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word «booby» has several, so you cannot guess it from the word alone. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «Male blue-footed boobies show off their blue feet in a dance.» Birds, feet and dancing are the clues, so a booby here is a seabird. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Old stories may call someone a booby, which means a silly person. A booby trap is a hidden trap that looks harmless. A booby prize is a joke prize for coming last. Each time, the words around the word decide the meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so check the clues before you decide.
fact: A booby is a large tropical seabird with bright blue or red feet that dives into the sea to catch fish.
fact: A booby trap is a hidden trap that catches someone who touches something that looks harmless.
fact: Some meanings of words are rude slang and are not for school; if you meet one, ask a trusted adult.
exercise: «Male blue-footed boobies show off their blue feet in a dance.» What is a booby in this sentence? | A joke prize for coming last | A hidden trap | A silly or stupid person | *A large tropical seabird that dives for fish
exercise: Old-fashioned story: «Tom called his little brother a booby for dropping the cake.» What does booby mean here? | A seabird | *A silly person | A hidden trap
exercise: «The hikers were careful, because a booby trap could be hidden under the leaves.» What is a booby trap? | *A hidden trap that looks harmless | A kind of seabird | A joke prize for coming last
test: «The sea was full of boobies diving for fish.» What does booby mean here? | A hidden bomb | A joke prize | *A seabird | A silly person
test: «Ella won the booby prize for coming last in the race, and everyone laughed.» What is a booby prize? | A bright blue bird | *A joke prize for coming last | A hidden trap | A dance
exam: Jayden reads «The booby trap was hidden under the grass.» What does the word trap tell you about booby? | *It is a hidden trap that looks harmless | It is a silly person | It is a prize for winning | It is a seabird that dives for fish
